    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d142">

                <pb facs="0200" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg135"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/4433: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-15T10:00:00+01:00">May 15, 1936—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 16—8:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>173. The Secretariat issued last evening a communication from the Chilean
                        representative<anchor n="40" xml:id="d142-f1"/> in which it is stated, “My
                    Government is of the opinion that in view of the recent events which have put an
                    end to the war between Ethiopia and Italy, it would be proper to discontinue the
                    economic, financial and other measures decided upon in connection with this
                    conflict”.</p>
                <p>In view of this communication being in terms of a proposal it is not known here
                    whether Chile has actually discontinued the sanctions measures.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
